      "question": "A point (3, -2) is rotated 180° counterclockwise around the origin. What are the new coordinates?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "(3, 2)",
        "B": "(-3, 2)",
        "C": "(-3, -2)",
        "D": "(2, 3)",
        "E": "(-2, -3)"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "180° rotation around origin: (x, y) → (-x, -y). So (3, -2) → (-3, 2).",
      "steps": [
        "1. 180° rotation formula: (x, y) → (-x, -y).",
        "2. Apply to (3, -2): → (-3, -(-2)) = (-3, 2)."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Rotation formulas: 90° CCW: (x,y)→(-y,x); 180°: (x,y)→(-x,-y); 270° CCW: (x,y)→(y,-x)."
